WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Industry leaders from Enthropic, OpenAI, and DeepMind align on pacing frontier development with shared safety evaluator access. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 172. Enthropic Chief Executive Dario Amode released an essay titled, We Must Paste the Frontier. The essay outlines a three-part plan for slowing AI development. Amode announced that Enthropic will give third-party evaluators permanent employee-level access

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:50.520
to its systems. Evaluators can verify safety measures, report incidents, and assess model alignment during training. Sam Altman replied that OpenAI agrees on pacing the frontier after recent internal discussions. OpenAI will implement the same independent evaluator access with more details coming soon.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:01:12.860
Demis Hassabis stated that the essay points toward the right path forward even though details need working through. Hassabis referenced DeepMind's recent proposal for an industry-wide standards body for frontier AI. The commitments respond to rising risks and aim to establish verifiable standards across frontier labs through shared evaluator access.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:23.620
Last week, OpenAI revised Astra benchmarks while other models scores fell, then rolled out faster multi-turn image editing with consistent subject preservation.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:33.200
Mestral closed Europe's largest venture round at a $24 billion valuation, giving builders a new, well-funded, open-weight contender.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:43.180
Enthropic detailed how sophisticated actors attempted cyber-attacks, influence operations and bio-weapons with Claude, and how every attempt was stopped.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:51.040
OpenAI shared its full defense factory architecture for continuous agent loops that find, validate, and fix vulnerabilities.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:02:03.800
A developer has prepared a 9.4 billion-parameter dense model incorporating N-gram tables, moonshot attention residual modeling, and rope over no-plaring at a 3-to-1 ratio.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.260
The model uses the LAMMA-3 tokenizer and language model head as a starting point.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:17.580
Training ran on low-git-level extraction from LAMMA-3 teacher model on a single RTX 4,090-plus rented hardware.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.180
The model remains stable after initial training steps.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:29.180
The author plans to switch the target to the OLOMO-3 series to avoid LAMMA licensing restrictions on synthetic data.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:34.380
All code, data, and weights will be released publicly once pre-training completes.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.260
Training code is optimized to run on a single RTX 6,000-pro series card.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:48.900
Chat GPT work with GPT-6 Astra generates 5,000 and 10,000 running routes from any address using OpenStreetMap.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:03:07.040
The system accepts an address, queries Nominatim for location, pulls local roads and trails via Overpass, calculates circular loops locally, and returns both an embedded D3 visualization and downloadable GPX and GOJS on files after running for 27 minutes.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:17.340
The visualization skill produces a self-contained HTML file using D3 from an allow-listed CDN that renders the route directly in the chat interface.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:28.280
Andre Carpathi noted that training on Stack Overflow would have demonstrated earlier that large language models can function as promptable general-purpose question-answering engines.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:37.880
A new platform called Lorevo hosts multiple Lora adapters on a single-base model GPU instance by loading adapters into memory on demand.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:43.860
The service exposes OpenAI compatible endpoints directly from the web app or CLI.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:53.500
Lorevo currently runs QN 3.54 billion for free with a 32,000 context window and collects only token counts and timestamps.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:04:07.380
The reverse engineered chat GPT visualized skill outputs a self-contained HTML fragment that uses D3 to draw both the base map and the overlaid route geometry stored in a JS on script tag inside the HTML.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:19.440
External resources are restricted to a short allow list of CDNs including CDN.JSDeliver.net, ESM.SH and UNPKG.com.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:25.680
A new framework for multi-agent reinforcement learning addresses coordination failures in those settings.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:40.120
RoastMyHarness runs deep-swee benchmark tasks against both BearPie and user-modified harnesses, extensions, skills or agents.MD files to measure quality, token efficiency and cost changes.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:46.960
The tool is currently tested on Linux and remains a work in progress with a wizard available to set up Pi extensions.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:05:02.760
A developer is building a Rust and Tari desktop application using QEMU with WHPX on Windows and is seeking advice on QMP for lifecycle management and approaches for letting an AI agent interact inside the VM.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:10.000
Users reported that the hugging face library sends telemetry identifying the specific coding agent being used.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:19.600
Test the Lorivo platform with a rank 8 or rank 16 Laura on QN3.54 billion to see shared adapter serving in action.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:27.220
Run RoastMyHarness against your own Pi extensions to quantify whether they improve token efficiency on deep-swee tasks.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:35.920
Generate a running route from your own address with chat GPT work and GPT 6 Astra to explore the visualized skill output.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:41.300
Further details are expected from OpenAI on its independent evaluator program.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:50.040
Additional Western Lab open-weight models in the 120 billion range may appear as Chinese model restrictions tighten for some organizations.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:57.100
Community training runs on the announced 9.4 billion dense model could produce early checkpoints within weeks.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:04.360
Before we go, OpenAI is expected to release more details on how its new evaluator access will work in practice.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:08.500
You can pop the hood on Laura adapter sharing in inference servers.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:17.320
Inference servers can keep a single copy of base model weights in GPU memory while swapping lightweight adapter deltas for different users.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:25.800
Adapter matrices are orders of magnitude smaller than the base weights, so memory traffic stays low even when many adapters are active.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:34.120
VLLM already implements fused kernels that apply these deltas during the forward pass without materializing full weight copies.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:37.260
The tradeoff appears when adapter rank grows.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:45.840
Higher ranks increase both compute per token and the chance that the adapter no longer fits in the remaining GPU memory alongside the base model.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:51.920
Teams therefore choose low rank adapters when they need to serve dozens of fine tunes on one card,

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.180
and accept the modest quality drop that comes with rank 8-32.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:05.100
When the workload instead requires many high rank adapters or very different base models, the economics shift back toward dedicated instances.

